{# Test stub for upstream EasyAdmin form theme blocks.

   The real upstream `crud/form_theme.html.twig` uses custom Twig
   filters (`ea_as_string` etc.) that require the EasyAdminTwigExtension
   to parse. Booting that extension in a unit test would mean wiring
   AdminContextProvider services etc. — overkill for asserting our
   wrapper-and-delegate contract.

   So we provide minimal stubs that mirror the structure of the upstream
   blocks our theme delegates to:
   - `ea_numeric_filter_widget` → wraps comparison + value (+ value2 in
     a `data-ea-value2-of-comparison-id` div).
   - `ea_datetime_filter_widget` → reuses the numeric block (same
     contract upstream).

   The stubs render placeholder markup so our assertions can verify
   that:
   1. The bridge wrapper is around the upstream block output.
   2. Our buttons are appended *after* the upstream content.
#}

{%- block ea_numeric_filter_widget -%}
    <div class="upstream-stub form-widget-compound">
        {{- form_widget(form.comparison) -}}
        {{- form_widget(form.value) -}}
        {%- if form.value2 is defined -%}
            <div data-ea-value2-of-comparison-id="{{ form.comparison.vars.id }}" class="d-none">
                {{- form_widget(form.value2) -}}
            </div>
        {%- endif -%}
    </div>
{%- endblock -%}

{%- block ea_datetime_filter_widget -%}
    {{- block('ea_numeric_filter_widget') -}}
{%- endblock -%}
